---
import "../../styles/architecture.css";
import DiagramCard from "./DiagramCard.astro";
---

<div class="catalog-architecture" role="region" aria-labelledby="ans-assessment-title" tabindex="0">
<svg class="architecture-svg" viewBox="0 0 640 1399" role="img" aria-labelledby="ans-assessment-title ans-assessment-desc">
  <title id="ans-assessment-title">From an ANS request to a private assessment</title>
  <desc id="ans-assessment-desc">An administrator selects an exact entry from one approved source. The API admits a Job bound to that entry, source revision and loaded authority policy. A worker acquires bounded credential-free evidence and checks it under the current source and policy. The worker must still own the Job claim.

  Job completion, the private result and its audit evidence commit atomically. A private result read requires current authorization and a retained read audit before disclosure, then reports current applicability. A successful Job can contain negative checks. Ordinary discovery makes no receipt requests, and an assessment does not establish software trust, artifact integrity or rights.</desc>
  <defs><marker id="ans-assessment-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" /></marker></defs>
  <path class="svg-connector" d="M320 164 V234" marker-end="url(#ans-assessment-arrow)" />
  <path class="svg-connector" d="M320 355 V425" marker-end="url(#ans-assessment-arrow)" />
  <path class="svg-connector" d="M320 546 V616" marker-end="url(#ans-assessment-arrow)" />
  <path class="svg-connector" d="M320 760 V830" marker-end="url(#ans-assessment-arrow)" />
  <path class="svg-connector" d="M320 974 V1021" marker-end="url(#ans-assessment-arrow)" />
  <DiagramCard x={60} y={20} width={520} title={"Explicit assessment; default off"} tone="optional" lines={["Operator loads public keys, exact", "publisher domains and evidence policy", "Evidence cannot introduce trusted", "keys or network authority"]} />
  <DiagramCard x={60} y={234} width={520} title={"1. Select one exact entry"} lines={["Use a current indexed entry or direct live selection", "Bind original bytes and source revision", "If the entry changed or is unavailable, select again"]} />
  <DiagramCard x={60} y={425} width={520} title={"2. Accept a bound Job"} tone="core" lines={["Check current request authority and loaded policy", "Retain exact entry, source and policy bindings", "Accepted does not mean assessed"]} />
  <DiagramCard x={60} y={616} width={520} title={"3. Acquire and check evidence"} lines={["Use bounded, credential-free fetches", "Keep signature, inclusion, target and status results separate", "Recheck the source and policy", "Verify that the worker still owns the Job claim"]} />
  <DiagramCard x={60} y={830} width={520} title={"4. Commit the private result"} tone="authority" lines={["Commit result, Job completion and audit atomically", "The source and policy must still match", "The worker must still own the Job claim", "Audit failure rolls back completion"]} />
  <DiagramCard x={60} y={1021} width={520} title={"5. Read the private assessment"} lines={["Check current authorization and", "retain a read audit before disclosure", "Return original evidence and current applicability", "A failed audit blocks disclosure"]} />
  <DiagramCard x={60} y={1235} width={520} title={"Completed checks can have negative results"} tone="warning" lines={["Job success does not mean the evidence passed each check", "Ordinary discovery makes no receipt requests", "Software trust, artifact integrity", "and rights remain not_assessed"]} />

</svg>
</div>
